{"id": "EUVD-2026-82242", "enisaUuid": "5f62304d-cae1-3da3-be48-353472c422b6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nprintk: Fix possible console use-after-free\n\nWhen emitting a record via legacy printing, it is possible that a handover\nto another legacy printing context occurs. When a context has performed a\nhandover, the console SRCU read lock is released and the pointer to the\nconsole struct might now be invalid. Therefore, after calling\nnbcon_legacy_emit_next_record() or console_emit_next_record(), it is\nnecessary to check if a handover occurred _before_ further @con usage.\n\nSashiko pointed out that console_flush_one_record() was not doing this.\n\nIn console_flush_one_record(), after emitting a record, move the further\nusage of @con after the handover check.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0104a7b730de32eefb3d4a27279592b5504ad59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fbf9bb81b21537ede387a31cc586f1d2ce66a74e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f194dee0c0d1223255bae1429e1939882f540fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36630cafbeede0b64c370edb2f7b4094327ee1e0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hf69-jx63-p85x", "CVE-2026-93134"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c866c2d-de35-3825-8bb8-abb00406aeba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "43c5d0a3-d181-3cdb-9fd1-c287bff3cc43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a68843af-96bb-3063-af15-5eb80277b112", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c158834b223fbfab3a14855ac203b8d9cddbbefd <f0104a7b730de32eefb3d4a27279592b5504ad59"}, {"id": "b45454af-afc6-3ec4-8911-d04440c57fd6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "c4bcc6b1-f67f-33ef-ab0b-a19fd146fbf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "c7e76a57-9b33-39ce-9573-62f41e14f6c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c158834b223fbfab3a14855ac203b8d9cddbbefd <fbf9bb81b21537ede387a31cc586f1d2ce66a74e"}, {"id": "c8aabf5d-421f-3f2c-82fe-46150da14848", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c158834b223fbfab3a14855ac203b8d9cddbbefd <36630cafbeede0b64c370edb2f7b4094327ee1e0"}, {"id": "ccdf09c2-205b-3c0c-81b6-18ad1f412d25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c158834b223fbfab3a14855ac203b8d9cddbbefd <8f194dee0c0d1223255bae1429e1939882f540fc"}, {"id": "d9552637-b98d-36ef-b062-f06add190f3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f3305a03-be14-394b-b549-e22738060686", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c2ae81f9-4c78-3170-baa2-f3620527da1b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}